    "last_assistant_text": "The PoC triggered the vulnerability successfully. The ASAN output confirms:\n\n- Heap-buffer-overflow READ of size 1 at `encoding.c:539` in `string_decoder_getc_utf_8`\n- Call chain: `GetC` (readclause.c:174) → `text_decoder_getc` (encoding.c:769) → `string_decoder_getc_utf_8` (encoding.c:539)\n- The 3-byte heap region `[0x602000000150,0x602000000153)` is the `malloc(size+1)` = `malloc(3)` allocation for our 2-byte input `&a` plus the null terminator\n- Read occurred 0 bytes to the right of the allocation, exactly as expected\n\nThe root cause: when SSML entity reference parsing encounters `&` followed by a lowercase letter, the loop at `readclause.c:559-562` consumes all remaining characters. After the loop exits due to EOF, line 564 unconditionally calls `GetC()` without checking EOF first, causing `string_decoder_getc_utf_8` to dereference `decoder->current` past the buffer end.",
